sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary) + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High (independent second assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Streichan et al. (2018), Mayer et al. (2010), Lefebvre et al. (2023) & Brauns et al. (2024) Drosophila global morphogenetic flow, curved-surface active nematic myosin mechanics & cell intercalation — MorphoEval overall 91.0/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 3 re-score of `2018-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow.py` (91.0/100, down from 92.3 in Pass 2). Both v2 remediation items were implemented in honest reduced form: (1) the compressible Stokes-Brinkman force balance is now also solved on the prolate spheroid $x^2/a^2 + (y^2+z^2)/b^2 = 1$ ($a = 250$, $b = 105\\ \\mu$m) by minimising the covariant dissipation functional assembled from the exact embedded strain $e_{ab} = \\tfrac12(\\mathbf{e}_a\\cdot\\partial_b\\mathbf{v} + \\mathbf{e}_b\\cdot\\partial_a\\mathbf{v})$, so the Gaussian-curvature term $-\\eta K \\mathbf{v}$ ($K = a^2/g_{ss}^2$) emerges without hand-derived Christoffel symbols; the sphere-limit gradient mode $\\nabla P_2$ reproduces the analytic eigenvalue $(\\eta+\\eta_b)\\,l(l+1)/R^2 - 2\\eta/R^2 + \\xi$ with residual $5.8\\times10^{-3}$ at $56\\times48$ and observed order 2.04; the closed surface generates the pole-return circulation intrinsically (curved-vs-cartographic WT $r = 0.833$); a Lefebvre-2023-type strain-rate positive feedback $m_{n+1} = m_0[1 + \\beta\\max(0,-e_{\\phi\\phi})/e_{\\rm ref}]$ converges to $m^*/m_0 = 1.70$ at loop gain $g = 0.358$ (bounded iff $g < 1$, Theorem 5); (2) a 240-junction T1/rosette ledger on a $10\\times24$ trunk lattice driven by the continuum cable myosin and DV contraction yields 125 collapses (72 simple T1 + 24 rosettes, largest 10 cells), median shrink time 7.75 min, and a tension-isogonal split $\\lambda_{\\rm total} = \\lambda_{\\rm int}\\lambda_{\\rm shape} = 1.52\\times1.26 = 1.92$ (intercalation share 0.64). Three new Lean 4 theorems (6 total, 0 sorrys) and 4 new measurements (11 total) were added. The score nevertheless decreases because the remediation exposed that the Pass 2 headline flow correlation is synthesised from the empirical $r$ (L1046-L1055), the morphospace map is an analytic surrogate (L1105-L1112), and the curved solver is not yet used for the 6-regime benchmark. Overall 91.0/100 (faithfulness 90.1, reproducibility 93.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit f18e3533; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 91, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 93, Reproducibility package 94. Output judged: docs/media/global_morphogenetic_flow_comparison.png: rendered output of 2018-streichan-global-morphogenetic-flow.py at f18e3533, image/png, 890697 B, 2464×1470 px, artifact_sha256 c2b12d9cc11f49cbc76202021e27a120ea25ff2713abd4ee312c77cb90e82127 (sha256 c2b12d9cc11f49cbc76202021e27a120ea25ff2713abd4ee312c77cb90e82127), spec_fingerprint c6f91e927b85c9e6c96461d53e4ae9c082d9c0ad9d74ed650b6b2f21fb08b782. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c6f91e927b85c9e6c96461d53e4ae9c082d9c0ad9d74ed650b6b2f21fb08b782; artifact_sha256: c2b12d9cc11f49cbc76202021e27a120ea25ff2713abd4ee312c77cb90e82127; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/global_morphogenetic_flow/drosophila_germband_extension_specimen.jpg=2d7fad8f57edcadf..., datasets/global_morphogenetic_flow/global_morphogenetic_flow_reference.json=160ead86ff9c447b..., datasets/global_morphogenetic_flow/scout_manifest.json=990f3ea83019f3d1...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-global-morphogenetic-flow-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Streichan, Lefebvre, Noppe, Hufnagel & Shraiman (2018) eLife 7:e27454 compressible viscous Stokes-Brinkman PDE eta*nabla^2 v + eta_b*nabla(nabla.v) - (eta/ell_H^2)*v = -nabla.sigma^a demonstrating that DV-polarized junctional Myosin-II cables plus isotropic posterior midgut invagination predict >90% (r = 0.924) of global embryonic tissue velocity | Mayer et al. (2010) Nature 467:617-621 hydrodynamic screening length ell_H = sqrt(eta/xi); Lefebvre et al. (2023) eLife 12:e78787 geometric/mechanical control of Myosin-II orientation and recruitment on the ellipsoidal embryo; Brauns et al. (2024) eLife 13:RP95521 tension-isogonal decomposition of convergent extension into cell rearrangement (T1/rosette) and cell-shape parts; Bertet et al. (2004) / Blankenship et al. (2006) junction shrinkage and 5-11-cell rosettes; reconstructed_in_script: 64x48 2D spectral Helmholtz compressible Stokes-Brinkman solver on the 500x420 um cartographic domain (Green's function L2 error 3.6e-16), 6-regime wild-type/mutant benchmark and 30 min Lagrangian marker advection (unchanged from Pass 2) | Pass 3: 56x48 (s, phi) finite-difference solver of the same force balance ON the prolate spheroid a = 250, b = 105 um using the exact embedded covariant strain, metric and Gaussian curvature K = a^2/g_ss^2 (sphere-limit analytic residual 5.8e-3, order 2.04; curved-vs-cartographic WT vector correlation r = 0.833; 31% of nodes carry intrinsic pole-return flow), strain-rate positive-feedback myosin recruitment to its fixed point (g = 0.358, m*/m_0 = 1.70), and a 240-junction T1/rosette ledger with tension-isogonal split (125 collapses, 24 rosettes up to 10 cells, median shrink 7.75 min, intercalation share 0.64) | Automated computer-vision contour, pair-rule stripe, DV cable gradient anisotropy, and posterior midgut invagination fold segmentation on drosophila_germband_extension_specimen.jpg (IDR0151, AP/DV = 2.3853 vs 2.3810 biological, 8 stripes, spacing = 75.86 px, solidity = 0.9383); transfer_boundary: Reduced curved-surface continuum: finite differences (not FEM) on a truncated (s, phi) grid with 20 um pole caps held at v = 0, single velocity-scale calibration to the 6.40 um/min WT peak, one-way myosin -> flow -> junction coupling; ledger rate constants calibrated to the Bertet (5-10 min) and Brauns (0.5-0.8) windows; does_not_claim: A predictive (uncalibrated) flow-correlation against measured PIV fields, two-way vertex-continuum coupling, 3D yolk/vitelline fluid-structure interaction, or digitised values for the Bertet/Blankenship/Brauns anchors (verified_offline = false)." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Close the loop between the intercalation ledger and the continuum: feed the T1-driven lambda_int back into the Lagrangian extension (currently lambda_shape = lambda_total/lambda_int < 1 during the first ~10 min, Panel F) and let junction collapse modify the local active stress (two-way coupling; L883-L995 is one-way).",
            "remediation needed: Replace the Dirichlet pole caps of the surface solver (L523-L527, L650-L654) with a closed-surface discretisation (e.g. a pole-regular grid or a triangulated FEM) and add a Killing-field test (rigid rotation must have zero viscous dissipation) to the self-test.",
            "remediation needed: Replace the synthetic flow-correlation construction in `evaluate_all_regimes` (L1046-L1055: `obs_unit` is built from `emp_r`, so r = 0.924 is reproduced by construction) with a correlation against a vendored/digitised observed velocity field (Streichan 2018 Fig. 2 PIV or the IDR0151 time series), and compute the 6-regime r from it.",
            "remediation needed: Run the 6-regime benchmark and the (ell_H x eta_b/eta) morphospace on the curved-surface solver instead of the flat pipeline: delete the ad hoc pole-return term (L404-L416) and the phenomenological `target_v_ap` rescaling (L422-L431), and replace the closed-form Gaussian morphospace (L1105-L1112) with solver output.",
            "remediation needed: Verify the Bertet 2004 / Blankenship 2006 / Brauns 2024 anchors and DOIs online, replace the recollected windows in `intercalation_reference.json` (verified_offline = false) with digitised values, and stop calibrating k_shrink/m_half to them." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.91"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
}

